  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{7}-6{x}^{5}-2670x$ at the point where $x=3.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)={x}^{7}-6{x}^{5}-2670x.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is equal to ${f}^{\u2032}(3).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7}-6{x}^{5}-2670x) \\\\  & =7{x}^{6}-30{x}^{4}-2670.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(3) & =7(3{)}^{6}-30(3{)}^{4}-2670 \\\\  & =5103-2430-2670 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $3.$",
